{"id": "EUVD-2026-99010", "enisaUuid": "0697665a-cceb-3c62-aeb8-10752fa2d2d8", "description": "Shaarli through 0.16.9 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows authenticated users to make the server request internal addresses by fetching bookmark thumbnails without private-address checks. Attackers can create bookmarks pointing to loopback, private, or cloud metadata addresses and trigger ThumbnailsController::ajaxUpdate or saving to send blind GET requests, with open_shaarli exposing this to any visitor.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:50:10", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/shaarli-open-mode-thumbnail-fetch-ssrf", "https://github.com/shaarli/Shaarli/blob/bfeadb4e5856702c05279bb2a5c405f2ed802015/application/front/controller/admin/ThumbnailsController.php#L46-L64", "https://github.com/shaarli/Shaarli/blob/bfeadb4e5856702c05279bb2a5c405f2ed802015/application/Thumbnailer.php#L82-L98", "https://github.com/shaarli/Shaarli", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/shaarli-through-0.16.9-ssrf-via-thumbnail-retrieval-update-thumbnail-route"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110225", "GHSA-w44p-6p6v-f82x"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "67e920e8-56a6-366f-be3b-77471543b822", "product": {"name": "Shaarli", "vendor": {"name": "Shaarli"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.16.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fc8c3983-d328-3e67-a655-4d1301eabcfd", "vendor": {"name": "Shaarli"}}], "isExploited": false}